ystem OS packages only; `python3 --version` \\u2192 3.14.4; `pip download jax` and direct `urllib` to pypi.org \\u2192 network failure (DNS), confirming offline; `nvidia-smi` \\u2192 driver communication failure, no /dev/nvidia*, `gpu_enabled=false` in metadata (host has CUDA 13.1 toolkit + driver 595.71.05 sources but no exposed device); `os.sched_getaffinity` \\u2192 224 CPUs; `free -g` \\u2192 ~2 TB RAM; no pip cache or relevant wheels found.\", \"assumptions\": [\"A designated GPU host (single CUDA GPU, model to be reported, e.g., A100-class) is assumed for the JAX side, since this runtime exposes no GPU\", \"The CPU baseline runs single-threaded on the same host with OMP_NUM_THREADS=1; multi-process CPU baselines are out of scope unless the researcher rules otherwise\", \"'Original CPU-based counterpart' = PettingZoo MPE simple_spread_v3 (the JaxMARL paper's own CPU baseline); original openai/mpe optional\", \"Environment defaults from JaxMARL source: simple_spread, num_agents=3, Discrete(5) actions, max_episode_length=100, autoreset, float32\", \"JAX timing mirrors JaxMARL's official bench/ scripts: device-side random actions inside a jitted vectorized step unroll, warmup discarded, block_until_ready synchronization\", \"Steps-per-second primary metric = env transitions/s summed over vectorized envs; agent-steps/s reported secondarily\", \"The eventual run happens on a prepared host with Python 3.10/3.11 and pinned jax/flax/jaxmarl/pettingzoo installs \\u2014 not in this 3.14 sandbox\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether the researcher wants the headline ratio at a fixed num_envs or as a sweep over num_envs (changes the reported speedup by orders of magnitude)\", \"Whether 'original counterpart' should strictly mean openai/mpe (harder to install, older physics-faithful but slower gym stack) rather than PettingZoo mpe v3\", \"Exact GPU device class we may attribute to the JAX number, and whether a CPU-only JAX x224-thread control run is also wanted as a third data point\", \"Whether observation/action handling overhead should be included symmetrically (my proposal) or minimized on both sides\", \"JaxMARL/paper throughput figures could not be verified locally (network off); any expected-order-of-magnitude figures must be cited from the paper, not measured here\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
